      "id": "chapter-10",
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Chapter 10 \u2014 Expand the Product Only After the Core Value Is Working",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The source ends by describing Searchable's next product direction: an autonomous AI agent intended to help businesses strategise and execute work required to improve their business and AI-search presence.\n\nThis is a product expansion thesis. The transcript does not provide implementation details, agent architecture, evaluation methods, or proof of the future product's performance.\n\nThe general lesson is to expand from a proven workflow into adjacent customer jobs.",
        "10.1 A sensible expansion sequence\n1. Make the original core feature reliable.\n2. Understand why customers return.\n3. Identify adjacent tasks customers already perform.\n4. Test whether customers want help with those tasks.\n5. Prototype one adjacent capability.\n6. Measure whether it improves customer outcomes.\n7. Integrate it into the workflow only when it adds clear value.\n\nFor an AI product, be especially careful about: accuracy and verifiability; data permissions and privacy; human review for consequential actions; clear limits on what the system can do; monitoring failures and unexpected behaviour; user control over automated actions; transparent reporting of what the AI did.\n\nAn autonomous agent is not automatically more valuable than a focused tool. The product should earn the right to automate more by first demonstrating that it can solve the original problem reliably.",
        "10.2 Hiring and organisational growth\nThe source reports that the company reached a team of 18 and hired into product, engineering, and marketing as revenue grew.\n\nHiring should follow bottlenecks, not vanity. Before adding a role, identify:\n- Which work is consistently delaying the business?\n- Is the work recurring and important?\n- Can the process be improved or automated?\n- Does the team have enough evidence to define the role?\n- Who will manage and evaluate the new hire?\n- Can the business support the cost under conservative assumptions?\n\nThe founding team should gradually replace heroic individual effort with clear processes, documented ownership, and reliable operating rhythms."
      ]
